","type":"text/x-markdown","caption":"outline"},"/home/runner/work/tw-plugin-library/tw-plugin-library/wiki/plugins/rimir/outline/README.md":{"title":"/home/runner/work/tw-plugin-library/tw-plugin-library/wiki/plugins/rimir/outline/README.md","text":"# Outline

Work on an ordinary tiddler like on a Streams outline: select a block, edit it in place, move it with Alt-Up/Down, indent it with Tab, and see the result rendered at once. The tiddler stays one tiddler; no helper tiddlers are created.

## Features

- **Always there, idle until used** - no button, no switch: Ctrl-Click (Cmd-Click on Mac) on a block of any wikitext tiddler wakes its outline. Until then the tiddler behaves exactly as without the plugin and costs as good as nothing. Escape with nothing selected, a click outside the tiddler or closing it puts it back to sleep.
- **Same rendering** - the tiddler renders exactly as usual; outline mode only adds data attributes, a selection frame and key handling.
- **Units** - list items, lists, headings (with sections), paragraphs, code blocks, tables, opened HTML containers, transclusion lines, and widgets or macro calls (one opaque unit each).
- **Type badges** - a small, faint label next to every unit shows what it is (paragraph, h2, code-block, bullet, ...), also on the editor field; they take no space. Settings: all (default), headings only, off.
- **Selection** - click, Up/Down, Left/Right to the parent / first child, Escape clears.
- **Move** - Alt-Up/Alt-Down swap a unit with its sibling, subtree included. Headings and blocks also move across heading lines: a new heading moves up over the blocks above it, a paragraph moves into the next section.
- **Indent** - Tab/Shift-Tab demote/promote list items and headings with their subtrees.
- **In-place editor** - Enter or a double-click opens TW's own edit widget at the unit: a compact one-line field by default, optionally the full editor with toolbar. Lists and headings are edited without their marker; nesting stays with Tab/Shift-Tab. Ctrl-Enter saves, Enter saves and starts a new unit, Escape discards, Ctrl-Up/Down save and move the editor to the previous/next unit, Alt-Enter turns the unit into another type. In selection mode Ctrl-Enter starts a new empty unit below the selection.
- **Delete** - the Delete key removes the selection with everything below it, after a small yes/no menu (a heading: with its section or just the heading); list items without sub-items go at once (a setting).
- **Copy, cut, paste** - Ctrl-C, Ctrl-X, Ctrl-V move a unit with its subtree, also to another tiddler; through the system clipboard: formatted into e-mail or Jira, as wikitext into text fields; pasted into an outline a unit takes the level of the place.
- **Undo** - Ctrl-Z takes back the last changes made in the outline (deletes, moves, merges, splits, edits), Ctrl-Y redoes them; for the running session. In the editor too, as long as nothing is typed (after a split, merge or move from the editor).
- **Split and merge** - Enter in the middle of a list item splits it at the caret, at the start of a filled item or paragraph it opens an empty one above; Backspace at the start of an item joins it to the item above (an empty item is deleted), Delete at its end pulls the item below up, like in Streams.
- **Ranges** - Shift-Up/Down (or Shift-Click) select neighbouring units at the same level; moves, indent, delete, copy/cut and Externalize take the whole range.
- **Externalize** - the block menu moves the selected unit or range into its own tiddler (`<note>/parts/part1`, configurable) and leaves `{{...}}` in its place; sub-items go into a list transcluded in their parent bullet.
- **Block menu** - Alt-Enter (also in the editor, to turn the edited unit into another type): insert a new block of any type after or before the selection (also before or after a list item: a new first bullet), or turn the selection into another type: everything turns into everything, only content of several lines does not go into a one-line type (heading, list item). A new, still empty unit takes any type with Alt-Enter.
- **Pluggable block types** - the types are tiddlers tagged `$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType` (outline ships paragraph, headings 1-3, bulleted, numbered, quote, quote block, code); another plugin adds its own with one data tiddler, e.g. [rimir/graphviz](https://github.com/rimir-cc/tw-graphviz) and [rimir/mermaid](https://github.com/rimir-cc/tw-mermaid). Typed blocks (`$$$text/vnd.graphviz` ... `$$$`) are edited without their `$$$` lines.
- **Examples and docs for diagrams** - the code field of a diagram offers the format's examples (picking one replaces the code, the preview shows it) and a link to its documentation; plugins ship them as tagged tiddlers, you can add your own.
- **Diagrams in a bullet** - "Add to this item" creates a diagram tiddler (on the first save, named `<note>/graphs/graphviz1`, configurable) and transcludes it in the item; a double-click on the diagram (or Shift-Enter) opens its source with a live preview in an overlay.
- **Key overview** - press `?` in an outline (or its small ? button) for a table of all keys; the *keys* tab shows the same. Every key is configurable in the settings tab with TW's shortcut editor.
- **Transclusions** - a marker on `{{...}}` lines and an orange selection frame; Enter edits the line, Shift-Enter opens the transcluded tiddler in an overlay right there, its own outline where you work as always (a diagram: its source with a live preview; Ctrl-Shift-Enter: in the story); also for a bullet with a transclusion.
- **Safe writes** - every write is a splice of a known range; changed text is relocated or refused, never guessed.

## Prerequisites

- TiddlyWiki 5.4.0 or later (JS modules: server restart or reload needed after install)
- Optional: `rimir/theme`, `rimir/doc-template`

## Quick Start

1. Install the plugin and restart the server.
2. Open a wikitext tiddler and Ctrl-Click (Cmd-Click on Mac) a block in it.
3. Click a block; Up/Down select, Alt-Down moves, Tab indents.
4. Enter edits, Ctrl-Enter saves.
5. `?` shows all keys.

Wikitext only; Markdown is not supported yet. llm-inline `AI:` lines do not fire from outline edits.
","type":"text/x-markdown"},"$:/plugins/rimir/outline/block-types.js":{"title":"$:/plugins/rimir/outline/block-types.js","text":"/*\
title: $:/plugins/rimir/outline/block-types.js
type: application/javascript
module-type: library

Registry of block types: tiddlers tagged $:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType, in tag order. Outline ships its own as
shadows ($:/plugins/rimir/outline/blocktypes/*); other plugins add theirs the same way.

getBlockTypes(wiki)                  -> [type] (cached until the next tiddler change)
getBlockType(wiki, name)             -> type or null
typeForContentType(wiki, contentType) -> the typed type for a content type, or null

type: {title, name, caption, badge, behaviour, level, marker, open, close, contentType, starter, docs, contexts, inline,
       turnInto, singleLine, kind, make(content, nl)}
  docs       - a link to the format's documentation (shown with a diagram's code field, ui/diagram-tools)
Examples for a type are tiddlers tagged $:/tags/rimir/outline/Snippet with for: <type name> (ui/diagram-tools).
  behaviour  - paragraph | heading (level 1-6) | item (marker) | fenced (open, close lines) | typed (content-type:
               a $$$<content-type> ... $$$ block)
  kind       - the unit kind it produces: block, heading or item
  singleLine - heading and item: one source line (line breaks become <br>)
  contexts   - where it can be inserted: "block" and/or "item" (inside a list item)
  inline     - for the item context: "transclude" or a template with $content$
A tiddler without a name, with an unknown behaviour or without the fields its behaviour needs is skipped.

\*/
"use strict";

var utils = require("$:/plugins/rimir/outline/text-utils.js");

var TAG = "$:/tags/rimir/outline/BlockType",
	KINDS = {paragraph: "block", heading: "heading", item: "item", fenced: "block", typed: "block"};

exports.TAG = TAG;

function field(tiddler, name) {
	var value = tiddler.fields[name];
	return typeof value === "string" ? value : "";
}

// The type of a tagged tiddler, or null when it is broken
function makeType(tiddler) {
	var behaviour = field(tiddler, "behaviour"),
		type = {
			title: tiddler.fields.title,
			name: field(tiddler, "name").trim(),
			caption: field(tiddler, "caption") || field(tiddler, "name"),
			badge: field(tiddler, "badge"),
			behaviour: behaviour,
			level: parseInt(field(tiddler, "level"), 10) || 0,
			marker: field(tiddler, "marker").trim(),
			open: field(tiddler, "open"),
			close: field(tiddler, "close"),
			contentType: field(tiddler, "content-type").trim(),
			starter: field(tiddler, "starter"),
			docs: field(tiddler, "docs").trim(),
			contexts: $tw.utils.parseStringArray(field(tiddler, "contexts") || "block"),
			inline: field(tiddler, "inline"),
			turnInto: field(tiddler, "turn-into"),
			kind: KINDS[behaviour],
			singleLine: behaviour === "heading" || behaviour === "item"
		};
	if(!type.name || !type.kind) {
		return null;
	}
	switch(behaviour) {
		case "paragraph":
			type.make = function(c) { return c; };
			break;
		case "heading":
			if(type.level < 1 || type.level > 6) { return null; }
			var bangs = new Array(type.level + 1).join("!");
			type.make = function(c) { return bangs + " " + utils.toBreaks(c); };
			break;
		case "item":
			if(!/^[*#>]$/.test(type.marker)) { return null; }
			type.make = function(c) { return type.marker + " " + utils.toBreaks(c); };
			break;
		case "fenced":
			if(!type.open || !type.close) { return null; }
			type.make = function(c, nl) { return type.open + nl + c + nl + type.close; };
			break;
		case "typed":
			if(!type.contentType) { return null; }
			type.make = function(c, nl) { return "$$$" + type.contentType + nl + c + nl + "$$$"; };
			break;
	}
	return type;
}

// Cached in the wiki's global cache, which TiddlyWiki clears synchronously on every tiddler change
exports.getBlockTypes = function(wiki) {
	return wiki.getGlobalCache("rimir-outline-block-types", function() {
		var types = [], seen = Object.create(null);
		$tw.utils.each(wiki.filterTiddlers("[all[shadows+tiddlers]tag[" + TAG + "]!is[draft]]"), function(title) {
			var tiddler = wiki.getTiddler(title),
				type = tiddler && makeType(tiddler);
			if(type && !seen[type.name]) {
				seen[type.name] = true;
				types.push(type);
			}
		});
		return types;
	});
};

// The type named `name` in the list `types`, or null
exports.byName = function(types, name) {
	for(var i = 0; i < types.length; i++) {
		if(types[i].name === name) { return types[i]; }
	}
	return null;
};

// The typed type (a diagram) for tiddler type `contentType` in the list `types`, or null
exports.byContentType = function(types, contentType) {
	for(var i = 0; i < types.length; i++) {
		if(types[i].behaviour === "typed" && types[i].contentType === contentType) { return types[i]; }
	}
	return null;
};

exports.getBlockType = function(wiki, name) {
	return exports.byName(exports.getBlockTypes(wiki), name);
};

exports.typeForContentType = function(wiki, contentType) {
	return exports.byContentType(exports.getBlockTypes(wiki), contentType);
};
